title: Choosing Our Enemies
new-page: true
view-if: year <= 1930 and enemies_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; enemies_timer = 18
max-visits: 3
is-card: true
card-image: img/kpd_poster.jpg
tags: party_affairs

= Choosing our enemies

In our media and campaign materials, who should we consider as our main opponents?

[? if enemies != 0 : Previously, we had considered the [+ enemies +] as our prior enemies. Is a change of direction necessary? ?]

- @fascist: The social fascists of the SPD, the regular fascist of the NSDAP, and the hyper-conservative DNVP.
- @far_right: The far right - the NSDAP and DNVP.
- @nsdap: The NSDAP alone.
- @spd: The SPD.
- @bourgeois: The bourgeois parties - the Center, DDP, and DVP.
- @easy_discard

@fascist
choose-if: united_front_maintained >0
unavailable-subtitle: The retained united front idea prevents attacking the SPD.
on-arrival: enemies = "the fascists and social fascists"; marxist_leninist_strength += 5; right_opposition_strength += 5; conciliator_strength += 5; left_opposition_dissent -= 5; workers_spd -= 2; workers_nsdap -= 2; workers_dnvp -= 2; spd_relation -= 10

We attack the overt fascist and capitalist NSDAP and DNVP along with the SPD, who we accuse of bourgeois opportunism.

@far_right
on-arrival: enemies = "far right"; left_strength += 5; left_dissent -= 5; workers_nsdap -= 3; workers_dnvp -= 3;

The far right is universally disliked among the party, but some accuse the "social fascism" of the SPD to be equally dangerous.

@nsdap
on-arrival: enemies = "NSDAP"; neorevisionist_strength += 5; nazi_urgency += 1; workers_nsdap -= 4;

[? if nazi_urgency == 0 or nsdap_r < 10 : The NSDAP is a tiny party right now, with more bark than bite. Many in our party are questioning our choices. ?][? if nazi_urgency > 0 and nsdap_r >= 10 : The Nazis are the most urgent problem for us to deal with. ?]

@spd
choose-if: united_front_maintained >0
unavailable-subtitle: The retained united front idea prevents this.
on-arrival: enemies = "SPD"; left_opposition_strength += 5; left_opposition_dissent -= 8; marxist_leninist_dissent -= 5; spd_relation -= 15; workers_spd -= 4; conciliator_strength -=5; right_opposition_strength -=5

Attacking the social fascists is popular among the center and left of our party, though some would rather focus on the actual fascists

@bourgeois
on-arrival: enemies = "bourgeois parties"; left_strength += 8; left_dissent -= 5; dvp_relation -= 5; z_relation -= 5; kpd_relation += 5; reformist_dissent += 8; workers_z -= 3; coalition_dissent += 1

Our anti-bourgeois rhetoric is popular among the left, but may make it harder to build the coalitions that are necessary for government in the future.
